<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast> a prov:SoftwareAgent;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "delphisci dataset-resolvability assessor (Grok 4.7)";
    prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4948-9192>;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/usesModel> <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7-high-fast>.
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7-high-fast> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/LanguageModel>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Grok 4.7";
    dc:identifier "grok-4.7-high-fast".
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/levin-2024-memory-17--grok> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/LLMClaimAssessment>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Grok 4.7 on levin-2024-memory-17: not-empirically-resolvable, resolvability 0.23";
    dc:description "Comparative biology can show that anatomical development precedes nervous systems. That fact does not test the specific historical claim that behavioral intelligence evolved from morphogenetic competencies. Fossils and genomes lack a variable that would separate this origin story from its rivals, so the claim is not empirically resolvable with current data.";
    dc:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Proposed test with existing data: Phylogenies can order the appearance of multicellular development and of nervous systems, but that order does not distinguish derivation of behavioral intelligence from morphogenetic problem-solving from other accounts of how behavior evolved.";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast>;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/assessmentType> "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/evidenceAgainst> "Earlier appearance of development than of brains is predicted by many evolutionary stories.", "Morphogenetic problem-solving competency is not a character coded in comparative datasets.", "The cause cited, inevitability of mutation and injury, is not a separate observable.";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasConfidence> "0.64"^^xsd:double;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasScore> "0.23"^^xsd:double;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasVerdict> "not-empirically-resolvable".
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/levin-2024-memory-17--grok--analysis-feasibility> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/LLMClaimAssessment>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Analysis feasibility of levin-2024-memory-17 by Grok 4.7: 0.25";
    dc:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0-analysis-feasibility>;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast>;
